405 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 139 0 R/Pg 23 0 R/A[578 0 R 0]/K[6]>>
endobj

406 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(The designations and import bans in key consumer markets can affect trade volumes, and put pressure on the governments and companies in the affected economies to improve their conditions; on the other hand, they can harm legitimate small-scale miners if not designed appropriately or if they are applied indiscriminately.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

407 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 139 0 R/T(The Way Forward)/E(The Way Forward)/Pg 23 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

408 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(Given the importance of DRC cobalt, particularly, in the race to replace fossil fuels, labour conditions in African mining have a direct influence on the progress and image of the global transition to electric vehicles and renewable energy storage. As information about mining practices in and around the world's highest-risk sourcing areas of origin emerges, manufacturers are increasingly at risk to reputational and legal liability if their products are found to contain minerals associated with forced or bonded labour, and have an incentive to strengthen their due diligence efforts and also to invest in responsible sourcing initiatives as much as genuine efforts to clean up supply chains but not simply to avoid higher-risk sourcing areas.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

409 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 139 0 R/T(Consequences for the Global Energy Transition)/E(Consequences for the Global Energy Transition)/Pg 23 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

410 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(Solving the problem of forced labour in African mining will most likely need to be tackled from multiple angles. Improved and coordinated application of mandatory due diligence in key consumer markets can mitigate the risk of companies gaming the system by moving sourcing toward jurisdictions with looser requirements as well as, or instead of, better conditions. If traceability systems existed in the future, and were independent and certified by third parties, they could be expanded beyond the 3TG minerals that are currently covered by the majority of traceability schemes, to other minerals used in batteries, such as cobalt.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

411 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E( The formalisation of artisanal and small-scale mining combined with better pricing systems, community organization and credit provision for small-scale miners, other than through debt bondage, can lessen the risk of debt bondage for miners, rather than eliminate the practice. Building the capacity of labour inspectors, building infrastructure for occupational health and safety and providing access to education in mining communities would help overcome some of the root causes of child labour. Finally, ongoing cooperation between the producing states, importing states, mining companies, and the downstream manufacturers and civil society organizations is key, as there is no one individual solution in the supply chain.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

412 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 139 0 R/Pg 23 0 R/A[536 0 R 0]/K[13]>>
endobj

