endobj

425 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(1. What is the main cause of forced labour and exploitation in artisanal, small-scale and industrial mining in Africa and how is it different in these two?)/Pg 24 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

426 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(2. What are the ways in which existing due diligence frameworks, e.g., OECD Guidance and UN Guiding Principles, need to be further developed to include other minerals, such as cobalt and other battery minerals?)/Pg 24 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

427 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(3. Who should bear responsibility for mining, subcontracting, smelting and refining and downstream manufacturing and how should the responsibility be held?)/Pg 24 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

428 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(4. How to ensure that the traceability and certification systems in the chain support rather than marginalize legitimate artisanal miners, without eliminating them from existing markets?)/Pg 24 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

429 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(5. How should the role of producing states, importing states, regional and international organizations in monitoring compliance and technical and financial support for the reform be defined?)/Pg 24 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

430 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(6. What action should the Council take to reconcile the need for critical minerals in this fast-moving global energy transition, with the need to remove forced and child labour from mineral supply chains?)/Pg 24 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

431 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(7. How can remedies and compensation be put in place for workers who have already experienced forced labour or exploitation in the mining industry?)/Pg 24 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

432 0 obj
